    "title": "Temptation Island Season 2 Trailer Promises Netflix Drama for the History Books",
    "text": "Temptation Island is officially back on Netflix for Season 2, and it’s promising major drama and emotional chaos. In this new season, a new group of couples puts themselves through the ultimate relationship test as they head to paradise and allow themselves to be tempted by a bevy of beauties and buff boys.The Netflix reality TV series is making a returnThis marks the show’s second season on Netflix (and 10th season overall), and it looks like things are getting amped up even more. Host Mark L. Walberg (not the well-known actor) welcomes the couples to a tropical island where they’ll see if their relationship can handle them living apart with attractive singles all trying to seduce them. What could go wrong?At the end of the day, couples will have to decide if they want to stay together, leave alone, or begin a new relationship with someone they meet on the island. And, as usual, for Temptation Island, emotions are running high from the get-go! In a perfect analogy for the show, one of the featured leads is seen literally playing with fire.The trailer showed a series of explosive confrontations, tears, emotional breakthroughs, and lots and lots of partying. It looks like it’s going to be one of the show’s most intense chapters yet. And that’s saying a lot considering last season’s threesome.Plus, there’s the return of the Temptation Haven, which consists of two private huts in both the men’s and women’s villas. This allows participants to explore temptation without any cameras present. Yikes! The catch? Once someone goes in, a red light goes off in the opposite villa, alerting everyone that someone has entered but not revealing who.It’s all a recipe for crazy drama indeed!Temptation Island Season 2 drops on Netflix on April 10.TELL US – ARE YOU LOOKING FORWARD TO THE NEW SEASON? DO YOU THINK THE COUPLES ARE GOING TO MAKE IT?The post Temptation Island Season 2 Trailer Promises Netflix Drama for the History Books appeared first on Reality Tea.",
